1. Customer & Transaction Analysis Page
Overview & Purpose
Evaluates customer demographics, account growth trends, transaction volumes, channel preferences, and professional profiles across various regional segments.

Key Insights
Core Metrics: Managed a customer base of 1,000 active clients generating 335K in Net Cash Flow, 19M in Total Deposits, and 74M in Transaction Amount.

Demographic Balance: Exhibited an even gender split among account holders, with 50.3% Male (503 clients) and 49.7% Female (497 clients).

Customer Acquisition Trend: Client acquisition fluctuated steadily between 2016 and 2023, averaging around 100 new accounts per cycle, before experiencing a sharp decline entering 2024.

Transaction Distribution & Channel Usage: Out of 4,000 total recorded transaction actions, the majority originated from the Retail segment (2,418), followed by Mass (1,164) and VIP (418). Distribution across banking channels remains balanced across ATM (408), Online Banking (398), and Physical Branch visits (358).

Customer Job Profiles: The top 5 client professions are led by Retired individuals, followed by Engineers, Doctors, Consultants, and Accountants.
